      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later narration places the whole San Cha mountain between Zuo clan’s Leng Chan mountain and Che clan’s Fei Lai mountain. Those two clans had been expanding and competing at San Cha with intent to occupy it before the three kings inheritance ruined that plan. The same passage frames Southern Border as a land of a hundred thousand famous mountains and countless unnamed hills, and treats Che and Zuo as nearby forces who can finally commit most of their troops once the inheritance turns strange.",
      "chapters": [
        389
      ],
